{
  "id": 20,
  "name": "return_aware_balanced",
  "intent": "We adjust the parent's weights to better balance exploration and exploitation: increase regret weight to 0.10 for sharper mid-tour differentiation, reduce nearest_remaining penalty to -0.08 to allow more exploration, add a spread penalty of -0.03 to favor centrally located candidates, and slightly reduce the return distance weight to 0.20*(1+0.5*p) to prevent overemphasis late in the tour. The hypothesis is that these changes will improve uniform instance performance by reducing greediness and adding useful variance-based tie-breaking, while maintaining strong clustered and grid performance.",
  "tags": [
    "return_aware",
    "spread"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    rd = f['return_distance']\n    nr = f['nearest_remaining']\n    r = f['regret']\n    p = f['progress']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    spread = f['spread']\n    return -d + 0.20 * rd * (1 + 0.5 * p) + 0.10 * r - 0.08 * nr + 0.05 * cd - 0.03 * spread",
